{
    "background_story": "Wesson was a rugged miner who spent his life digging deep into the earth's crust. He had heard tales of a rare mineral called kernite, a borate mineral found in limited quantities. Wesson became obsessed with finding this elusive ore, convinced that it held the key to unlocking new technologies. He spent years searching, facing countless setbacks and disappointments. Finally, after a decade of searching, Wesson struck paydirt in a remote corner of Death Valley. His discovery of a vast kernite deposit sent shockwaves through the mining community, earning him a reputation as one of the greatest prospectors of his time. Wesson's perseverance and dedication to uncovering the secrets of the earth had paid off, and his name became synonymous with the rare and valuable mineral.",
